# L §5.14: "A movement whose day is a hole makes every flows and binding over a span it might fall in a hole"; L §5.11:
# "A key whose where is a hole is an unknown member: count is a hole; sum is a hole unless that key's term is known to
# be 0". pay's day pday has no row: the count and the sum over transfers in 2026 are holes. (Writer 5's T-59, stated.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input pday: date

move pay: transfers
  on pday
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask q1: count(x in transfers over 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31)
ask q2: sum(x.cash.amount for x in transfers over 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31)
=== expect
q1: ? ...
  cut 2026-12-31
q2: ? ...
  cut 2026-12-31
